From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ScarlettMac <scarlettmac@local>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:30:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] shader: key the cache on VICTORY_BARRIER_LDS and
 prototype sampleGrad

The shader cache key did not cover the diagnostic emitter switches, so
VICTORY_BARRIER_LDS=1 would have reused DXIL emitted with mode 1|2|8. Both
switches are now read once in victory_shader::emit::{barrier_lds,
ps_sample_grad} and hashed into the base key, like SOURCE_HASH.

VICTORY_PS_SAMPLE_GRAD=1 is the prototype for the AGX air.sample_ failure:
a pixel shader's implicit-LOD image_sample (op 60, not cubes or offsets
past the existing path) is emitted as sampleGrad (63) with derivCoarse
(83) of each coordinate for both directions. Off by default; the next run
with VICTORY_PS_SAMPLE_GRAD=1 tells whether the three mesh/pixel pairs
create. Host tests: the key test covers the two switches; victory-shader
passes.
